WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.880
Luffy might be in trouble.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.540
Bevause, as the One Piece manga is quickly
reaching the end of the Egghead Island Arc,

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:12.610
and this chapter just gave us hints of how
the final battle is truly going to play out.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.490
Which includes the POWERHOUSE MATCHUPS including
Gear 5 Luffy against the Shadow Clone Jutsu

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:25.449
Admiral Kizaru, the Awakened Lucci versus
Zoro, and Saint Saturn against probably everyone

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:26.449
else.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:30.369
But that’s not all because with most of
the major characters coming together on the

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:36.700
bottom part of the island whatever climactic
event we were promised is surely about to

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.180
blow up and turn this arc into the match that
sets the final saga burning.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:48.210
But first we just have to talk about Luffy
versus Kizaru because as I hoped the marine

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.050
admiral is not just going to be completely
overwhelmed by Gear 5 Luffy.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:59.699
In fact what I NEVER EXPECTED was to see Kizaru
bust out the Shadow Clone Jutsu and make clones

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:02.620
of himself in order to take out Luffy.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:10.060
In fact, up to now he honestly seems completely
unfazed by Gear 5 Luffy, apparently being

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:15.590
the only person to be fully resistant to Luffy’s
cartoon powers and even easily outsmarted

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.010
Luffy by distracting him with the clones.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.259
Not the first time we’ve said Luffy’s
been outsmarted, but it makes me wonder if

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:27.299
we, and even possibly Luffy, have been underestimating
Kizaru a bit.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:33.360
I mean this man is a marine admiral who confidently
asked if he should go to Wano to handle Kaido

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.450
AND BIG MOM&nbsp; so maybe we should be wondering
just how desperate this situation is for Luffy

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:49.920
and 

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:50.920
the crew.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:02:11.120
And while we 

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:18.989
will discuss more about the fights in this
chapter in just a moment, first I do have

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:22.310
one major question about Kizaru’s new clone
powers.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.050
I mean we have seen many devil fruit users
create clones before like when the string

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:32.550
fruit user Doflamingo made a clone to tank
this hit and we’ve Nico Robin make tons

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:38.110
of clones that she can control, but both of
these characters ate Paramecia type devil

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:42.370
fruits which allow them to control the substance
they produce.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:48.050
But that is not the case for Kizaru and as
far as we know Logia fruits have only ever

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:52.989
been able to shoot out their elemental abilities,
not really control them.

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:57.080
For example, the lightning fruit user Enel
could launch massive bolts of electricity

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:03.269
and admiral Akainu can blast people’s faces
off with his magma fists, but creating separate

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:05.769
clones that can act on their own?

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:13.030
That is something we have never seen and I
am SUPER CURIOUS what level of control Kizaru

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.270
has over these.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.879
For example, is he somehow controlling the
light?

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:22.819
Or are they independent beings that can act
on their own?

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:27.939
Or are they just light projections kinda like
the holograms we saw earlier in this arc?

00:03:27.939 --> 00:03:33.240
Plus we have to ask how this is even possible
in the first place since we have never seen

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.629
it before.

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:40.910
Maybe it is some form of awakening or is it
just some special ability on his light devil

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.910
fruit?

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:48.530
I honestly cannot wait to find out.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:53.690
Now despite how incredibly cool Kizaru looks
showing off even more of his awesome abilities,

00:03:53.690 --> 00:04:00.049
I have to say that I am actually pretty disappointed
in the direction this fight seems to be taking.

00:04:00.049 --> 00:04:08.300
Because it seems that Kizaru is not 100% interested
in fighting Luffy.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:13.770
Instead, he keeps going after his different
objectives, like when he tried to attack the

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.150
Vegapunks last chapter and in this one.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.500
Likewise, Luffy is busy trying to protect
his friends instead of going all out against

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.500
the admiral.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.979
Which, by the way, that shot of him taking
in Kizaru’s light and splitting it like

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:31.210
some kind of prism was just awesome.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.930
But besides that I am just getting a really
bad feeling that this fight is going to end

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:46.560
with the straw hats and some allies escaping
instead of the all out fight that I was personally

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.789
hoping for.

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:53.479
However, this might actually be a good thing
because we definitely won’t be getting a

00:04:53.479 --> 00:04:57.600
long-drawn out fight like we would expect
from a major battle.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:03.650
Need I remind you of the forty-nine chapter
marathon like Luffy versus Kaido?

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:15.940
And ultimately this means we should be getting
to the promised epic finale even faster.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.930
There is still plenty of fighting going on
in this chapter though and in particular one

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:26.870
MAJOR CLASH is Zoro against the fully awakened
leopard fruit user Lucci.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:32.550
And I’m honestly SUPER EXCITED to see how
Zoro stacks up against the government secret

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.550
agent.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:39.150
Because if Gear 5 Luffy absolutely destroyed
Lucci, then Zoro’s performance against Lucci

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:44.600
should give us a good idea of how current
Zoro compares to Luffy.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:49.150
Of course we do have to consider the small
chance that Zoro loses this battle, but honestly

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.979
I would be SHOCKED if that were to occur.

00:05:52.979 --> 00:05:58.419
Even in his awakened form, I don’t think
Lucci is stronger than Kaido’s right hand

00:05:58.419 --> 00:06:03.180
man, King, and if you remember Zoro basically
one-shotted King once he finally learned how

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.620
to control his advanced conqueror’s haki.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:12.259
Although Lucci is probably more of a backstabbing,
ruthless fighter than King, so who knows maybe

00:06:12.259 --> 00:06:17.729
he will use some dirty tricks instead of fighting
Zoro in a true one on one?

00:06:17.729 --> 00:06:23.400
And while we’re speculating about the future,
this is the perfect time to recap the possibility

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.750
of the Vegapunks leaving the island with the
straw hats.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:32.910
In fact, in this chapter Jinbe can even be
seen taking a bunch of Vegapunk’s gear towards

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:37.960
the Thousand Sunny, so it seems like a pretty
strong theory that at least one of the Vegapunks

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:42.370
will be coming along.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.660
And in case you forgot, here are the latest
updates on all seven Vegapunks.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.990
We know from chapter 1090 that Shaka and Pythagoras
were confirmed to be dead, although you know

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.940
how that goes in One Piece.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.340
Will of P and everything.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.720
Then we have the bite-sized Edison who is
still in the control room with Nami, Usopp,

00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.870
and the traitor York.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:04.310
Next is Lilith who is currently piloting Franky’s
giant mech carrying the straw hats ship to

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.330
the back of the island.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:11.060
And that just leaves Atlas and the main body,
who have driven this awesome “Vega Tank”

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:16.280
all the way to the battlefield to order the
Pacifistas back to their side.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:23.940
With all of them scattered around it is still
really hard to tell how many, if any, of these

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.480
Vegapunks will survive.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:32.879
Though if I had to bet I would guess Lilith
will be the one to go with the straw hats,

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:38.060
since she is the one who has been with the
ship all this time.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:43.620
But I simply cannot go any longer without
sharing this AWESOME theory about the main

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:49.540
Vegapunk which actually makes A TON of sense
for the epic finale for the end of this arc.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.540
Hear me out…

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:56.000
Because as we’ve discussed before, the Egghead
island arc has parallels to many previous

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:04.000
arcs, but one connection I have not heard
discussed as much is the similarities to the

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.370
island of Ohara which we saw during Robin’s
flashback.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:11.930
On that island there was a ton of information,
such as research into the poneglyphs, that

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.830
the World Government didn’t want anyone
to share with the rest of the world.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:21.370
So let’s bring this back to Egghead now,
we have the reverse situation where Vegapunk

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:26.920
has A TON of top secret information that he
most likely doesn’t want to fall into the

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.920
world government’s hands.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.620
On top of that, he also knows about the poneglyphs
and the ancient kingdom.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:37.570
So I can just imagine that as the straw hats
escape, the main Vegapunk does two things.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:42.589
First, he sends out information about the
ancient kingdom to the entire world, completing

00:08:42.589 --> 00:08:44.950
the work that was started at Ohara.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:50.330
He could probably do this using Punk Records,
which is kinda like the internet.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:56.610
Second, I can very easily see Vegapunk pushing
a self-destruct button or something to destroy

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:01.620
Egghead island just like the World Government
destroyed Ohara.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.090
He would probably do this to prevent the World
Government from getting their hands on the

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:09.410
Mother Flame energy source that they need
to power their super weapon that can destroy

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.850
entire islands.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:15.890
And if this sounds too crazy for you, remember
that Vegapunk installed a self-destruct button

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:22.060
on his previous lab on Punk Hazard, so it’s
actually not as insane as it sounds.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:29.390
And that mind-blowing situation is exactly
what Kizaru and Saint Saturn would want to

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.600
avoid.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:35.940
Because although this would most likely accomplish
their goal of killing Vegapunk, it would mean

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:41.600
their other two main objectives of obtaining
the Mother Flame and rescuing York are probably

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.600
ruined.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.640
Who knows maybe Saint Saturn might even be
caught up in the explosion which would be

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.880
a huge shock to the world.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:56.490
But speaking of Saint Saturn, his brief appearance
at the end of this chapter hopefully means

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.370
that he will soon be joining the action.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.380
Now what will this man be doing?

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:06.839
Well, let’s break it down because no matter
what way you look at it, he ABSOLUTELY MUST

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:12.209
be a part of the epic conclusion that we were
told would end Egghead Island.

00:10:12.209 --> 00:10:17.279
The first and most obvious thing he can do
is retake control of the Pacifistas after

00:10:17.279 --> 00:10:19.990
the Vegapunks took them over in this chapter.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.399
Which by the way, I have to ask where are
the Seraphim at this point?

00:10:22.399 --> 00:10:27.010
I know they were locked up in bubbles a few
chapters ago, but wouldn’t it make sense

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:31.029
for them to join the battle if they are commanded
by Vegapunk?

00:10:31.029 --> 00:10:35.860
Or maybe they should stay locked up in bubbles
to keep them from flipping sides AGAIN.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.950
And honestly I hate to add onto the negative
takes in this review but, I am starting to

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:44.820
get pretty tired of this whole Seraphim and
Pacifista flipping sides thing.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:51.440
Because when these Warlord clones were introduced
there was SO MUCH hype surrounding these characters.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:56.470
BUT all that hype is absolutely gone at this
point because one chapter they are our allies,

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:57.970
then in the next they are enemies.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:04.430
I mean yes they are super strong, but then
they were also taken out in one go by bubbles.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.580
Yeah…

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:10.700
Although the one side of this that I WOULD
LOVE TO SEE is the Seraphim somehow managing

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.240
to gain control of themselves.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:18.019
Which totally fits with all the talk in recent
chapters about being slaves to the government.

00:11:18.019 --> 00:11:23.510
For example, Kizaru feels like he has to follow
orders and Kuma used to be a World Government

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:24.510
slave.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:32.800
So wouldn’t it be great if the ones who
literally have to follow commands could somehow

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.089
break free?

00:11:34.089 --> 00:11:35.089
Whew.

00:11:35.089 --> 00:11:36.480
Anyway, rant over.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.480
Subscribe to the channel.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:38.970
And let’s get back to Saint Saturn.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:44.800
Now it should be easy for him to command the
Pacifistas because of the command structure

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.749
we were shown earlier in the arc.

00:11:46.749 --> 00:11:53.060
But besides that I NEED for Saturn to show
off the mysterious powers that we first saw

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.620
in chapter 1085.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:12:02.660
Because in case you forgot, Saturn appears
to have this bull-like transformation with

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.240
these giant horns.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:08.930
Now we don’t know if this is a devil fruit
power or something else, but I just have to

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:09.970
learn more about it.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:15.800
And what more perfect time than the end of
this arc when there is sure to be a massive

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:16.990
conflict.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:23.410
Speaking of that conflict, Sanji might actually
be the first one to face off against Saint

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:27.730
Saturn because he is currently with the main
Vegapunk and the Pacifistas.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.589
So how will Sanji respond to seeing the Elder
Star?

00:12:31.589 --> 00:12:35.899
Will he jump straight into an attack or will
he be busy fighting the Pacifistas?

00:12:35.899 --> 00:12:41.120
Or will someone else come and make a mess
out of this fight as well?

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:46.470
Honestly, this would be the perfect time for
the Blackbeard pirates to make their appearance.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:51.120
Although it would also be the perfect opportunity
for them to go after the rubbings of the Poneglyphs

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.350
on the Thousand Sunny, since it is only protected
by Lilith and Jinbe at this point.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:59.660
Or an even crazier option would be if someone
like the marine hunting organization Cross

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:04.550
Guild showed up and truly shocked the world
by taking out one of the Gorosei on their

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.550
own.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:06.550
Man, THAT.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.550
WOULD.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.550
BE.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:09.550
INSANE!

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.700
Plus it would give us the chance to see Luffy
and Buggy reunite.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:16.800
Which honestly I love these two together SO
MUCH that I made an entire video explaining

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:22.459
how stupidly powerful Luffy would be with
a second devil fruit, including Buggy’s

00:13:22.459 --> 00:13:24.730
surprisingly overpowered Chop-Chop fruit.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:29.080
And if you want to see just how insane it
gets with some of these wild combinations,

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.740
you can watch that video right here.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:35.370
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

